    <GaugingStation location="Rhayader" name="Wye" number="55005">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station. Natural flow regime. Closed and replaced by Ddol Farm (55026) in Oct 1969.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Bed gravel shoals, generally unstable. Above 2m flow overtops right bank and flows across playing fields. Two peak flow ratings applied across period of record, one pre and one post Apr-1946. No gaugings available. Upper limit at bank full as over-bank flow occurs. Ratings give markedly different flow at high stage even though datums identical; ratings therefore seen as unreliable.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station. Closed and replaced by Ddol Farm (55026) in Oct 1969 which has higher banks and is more contained.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural to within 10% at Q95.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Wet, upland catchment draining impermeable, metamorphosed Silurian sediments. High relief, headwaters reach over 600m, and feature steep sided and high gradient streams. Moorland and forestry.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Not gauged up to QMED. However, QMED is almost identical to that at 55026 in the same catchment." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Poor reliability at high flows. Recommended use of 55026 for pooling as it is located in the same catchment." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
